    <DataNode elementId="AT4G17050-MONOMER" textLabel="AT4G17050-MONOMER" type="Protein">
      <Xref identifier="Q680J5" dataSource="uniprot" />
      <Graphics centerX="300" centerY="215" width="90.0" height="25.0" textColor="000000" fontName="Arial" fontWeight="Normal" fontStyle="Normal" fontDecoration="Normal" fontStrikethru="Normal" fontSize="12" hAlign="Center" vAlign="Middle" borderColor="000000" borderStyle="Solid" borderWidth="1.0" fillColor="FFFFFF" shapeType="Rectangle" />
      <Comment source="pmngroup, PMN, dreher">The |FRAME: AT4G17050| gene, encoding |FRAME: AT4G17050-MONOMER|, has been discovered based on its functional association with the |FRAME: AT4G20070| gene and possession of a predicted ER targeting sequence |CITS: [19935661]|. The gene was cloned, expressed and purified. The purified protein showed no activity with |FRAME: ALLANTOATE| as substrate, but when combined with |FRAME: CPLX-7979|, the ammonium release was accelerated, and stoichiometric amounts of |FRAME: CPD-1091| were generated. When |FRAME: AT5G43600-MONOMER| was also added to the mixture, |FRAME: ALLANTOATE| was completely hydrolyzed to |FRAME: GLYOX| and |FRAME: AMMONIA| without a urea intermediate, confirming that |FRAME: AT4G17050| encodes an enzyme that converts |FRAME: CPD-598| to |FRAME: CPD-1091| |CITS: [19935661]|.</Comment>
